{"schemaVersion":1,"generatedAt":"2026-08-16T16:20:46.501Z","id":"5ec0823099ddf7146fe85e57","canonicalUrl":"https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260731152344.1905882-1-youssef.abdulrahman%40oss.qualcomm.com/","channels":["linux-arm-msm"],"thread":{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"thread:lore-git:20260731152344.1905882-1-youssef.abdulrahman@oss.qualcomm.com","source":{"kind":"static-generated","canonicalThreadUrl":"https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260731152344.1905882-1-youssef.abdulrahman%40oss.qualcomm.com/","fetchedAt":"2026-08-16T16:20:46.501Z","contentDigest":"lore-git:20260731152344.1905882-1-youssef.abdulrahman@oss.qualcomm.com"},"subject":"Re: [PATCH v2] accel/qaic: Address potential out-of-bounds read in resp_worker()","messages":{"96e73102-eced-4937-a622-6f2cb5a32ec1@oss.qualcomm.com":{"id":"96e73102-eced-4937-a622-6f2cb5a32ec1@oss.qualcomm.com","messageId":"96e73102-eced-4937-a622-6f2cb5a32ec1@oss.qualcomm.com","references":["20260731152344.1905882-1-youssef.abdulrahman@oss.qualcomm.com"],"missingAncestorIds":["20260731152344.1905882-1-youssef.abdulrahman@oss.qualcomm.com"],"author":{"name":"Jeff Hugo","address":"jeff.hugo@oss.qualcomm.com"},"replyTo":[],"to":[{"name":"Youssef Samir","address":"youssef.abdulrahman@oss.qualcomm.com"},{"name":"","address":"carl.vanderlip@oss.qualcomm.com"},{"name":"","address":"troy.hanson@oss.qualcomm.com"},{"name":"","address":"zachary.mckevitt@oss.qualcomm.com"}],"cc":[{"name":"","address":"ogabbay@kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"lizhi.hou@amd.com"},{"name":"","address":"karol.wachowski@linux.intel.com"},{"name":"","address":"ruikai@pwno.io"},{"name":"","address":"linux-arm-msm@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"dri-devel@lists.freedesktop.org"}],"timestamp":{"raw":"2026-08-14T19:11:46.000Z","iso":"2026-08-14T19:11:46.000Z","valid":true},"subject":"Re: [PATCH v2] accel/qaic: Address potential out-of-bounds read in resp_worker()","mailingLists":[{"id":"linux-arm-msm.vger.kernel.org","displayName":"linux-arm-msm.vger.kernel.org"}],"blocks":[{"kind":"quote","attribution":"On 7/31/2026 9:23 AM, Youssef Samir wrote:","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"Although 'commit 2feec5ae5df7 (\"accel/qaic: Handle DBC deactivation if the"},{"depth":1,"text":"owner went away\")' fixes the scenario it was intended for by walking the"},{"depth":1,"text":"message and only decoding QAIC_TRANS_DEACTIVATE_FROM_DEV, if present, it"},{"depth":1,"text":"skipped over the bounds checking code that is included in decode_message()."},{"depth":1,"text":"This could lead to issues such as reading past the slab allocation's end,"},{"depth":1,"text":"infinite loops or kernel panics. For those issues to happen, a malformed"},{"depth":1,"text":"wire message is needed to be sent from the device."},{"depth":1,"text":"> Instead of duplicating the bounds checking code already present in"},{"depth":1,"text":"decode_message(), use the function inside resp_worker()."},{"depth":1,"text":"> Reported-by: Ruikai Peng <ruikai@pwno.io>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Fixes: 2feec5ae5df7 (\"accel/qaic: Handle DBC deactivation if the owner went away\")"},{"depth":1,"text":"Reviewed-by: Jeff Hugo <jeff.hugo@oss.qualcomm.com>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Reviewed-by: Lizhi Hou <lizhi.hou@amd.com>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Signed-off-by: Youssef Samir <youssef.abdulrahman@oss.qualcomm.com>"}],"lineCount":14,"maximumDepth":1},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Applied to drm-misc-fixes."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"-Jeff"}],"patchIds":[],"attachmentMetadata":[],"sourceOrdinal":0,"diagnostics":[],"declaredParentMessageId":"20260731152344.1905882-1-youssef.abdulrahman@oss.qualcomm.com"}},"rootIds":["96e73102-eced-4937-a622-6f2cb5a32ec1@oss.qualcomm.com"],"childrenByParent":{},"chronologicalIds":["96e73102-eced-4937-a622-6f2cb5a32ec1@oss.qualcomm.com"],"patchSeries":[],"diagnostics":[],"patches":{}}}